From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Smith <scott@newtrostudios.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:40:02 -0400
Subject: remotesmith(0306): changing the permanent password ends sessions that
 used it

AC-39. Upstream leaves every session up when the host's password
changes, so a controller that logged in with the old password keeps
control. Each change of the stored permanent password (through the IPC
setter, or a config sync from the other process) now bumps an epoch. A
connection that authenticated with the permanent password remembers its
epoch, and its once-a-second timer closes it with a no-retry reason once
the epoch moved on (port-forward tunnels on their 30 s timer). The
no-retry close also drops its 30 s reconnect session, and the
controller's reconnect policy (0302) never retries that reason, so the
saved credential has to be updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
